cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "EPICS MCP"
abstract: >-
  A read-by-default Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives an AI
  assistant diagnosable access to an EPICS control system: live process-variable
  values over PVAccess and Channel Access, connection diagnosis with a per-plane
  explanation, and cross-plane provenance joining ChannelFinder, the EPICS
  Archiver Appliance, the Phoebus Alarm Logger, a naming service, IOC startup
  files and CS-Studio operator screens. It also reads and writes the Phoebus
  Olog logbook, which is a plane of its own that no analysis joins yet.
  Mutating operations sit behind independent, audited gates that are disabled
  by default.
type: software
authors:
